Romhack Camp Badge 2026
=======================

This repository holds two separately licensed firmware projects. They are built as
separate binaries into separate flash partitions and are never linked or combined into
one work, so their licences apply independently:

  firmware/tactility/   derived from Tactility (https://github.com/TactilityProject/Tactility)
                        Tactility/ and Firmware/ are GPL v3.0.
                        Modules/, and most of Devices/ and Drivers/, are Apache 2.0.
                        See firmware/tactility/LICENSE.md for the per-subproject breakdown
                        and firmware/tactility/Documentation/ for the licence texts.

  firmware/retro-go/    derived from Retro-Go (https://github.com/ducalex/retro-go)
                        GPL v2.0, except retro-core/components/handy (Lynx emulator, zlib).
                        See firmware/retro-go/COPYING.

  firmware/tactility/   **Doom Shareware v1.9** is copyrighted © 1993-1996 by **id Software / ZeniMax Media Inc.**
  Data/data/roms/Doom/  This file is **proprietary, copyrighted material** and is not covered 
  doom1.wad.zip         by this repository's open-source license.
                        It is bundled here in compliance with the original id Software Shareware 
                        License, which permits free, unmodified distribution of the   shareware 
                        data file for non-commercial evaluation.
                        No commercial use, modification of the WAD contents, or extraction of internal assets (textures, audio, maps) is permitted.

Doom® is a registered trademark of id Software / ZeniMax Media Inc. This project is unaffiliated with id Software.

Changes made for this badge are released under the licence of the file they modify.

Third-party components keep their own licences; each carries its COPYING, LICENSE or
NOTICE file alongside the source it applies to. firmware/tactility/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md
lists the ones vendored into that tree.

GPL v2.0 and GPL v3.0 are not compatible with one another. Nothing in this repository
combines code from the two trees, and the two firmware images do not share linkage,
headers or a build. Keep it that way.
